{"prototypeToken":{"displayName":20,"displayBars":20,"flags":{"pf2e":{"linkToActorSize":true,"autoscale":false}},"height":1,"width":1,"name":"Kolufs Krafsa","actorLink":false,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e/art/tokens/kolufs-krafsa.webp","scaleX":2,"scaleY":2,"tint":"#ffffff","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":null},"light":{"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1},"negative":false,"priority":0},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":true,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":2,"texture":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e/art/subjects/kolufs-krafsa.webp"}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"depth":1},"name":"Kolufs Krafsa","type":"npc","effects":[],"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":130,"temp":0,"max":130,"details":""},"ac":{"value":22,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":30,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"climb","value":20}],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"curse","exceptions":[]}],"weaknesses":[{"type":"silver","value":5,"exceptions":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common"],"details":"one additional language they knew before being cursed"},"level":{"value":6},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Kolufs krafsas are mammalian humanoids afflicted with a bizarre curse that transforms them into something else, a pupal stage on the path to something terrifying and new. As a part of that transformation into a nonmammalian creature, all the kolufs krafsa's hair falls out. For ancestries like dwarves that place great value on their thick, lustrous beards, the curse is especially horrifying.</p>\n<p>Curiously, kolufs krafsas don't always choose their victims randomly. Despite the burgeoning evil of the curse within them, they prefer to attack those who truly deserve it. Because of that, many kolufs krafsas respond to the pleas of oppressed commoners. A kolufs krafsa listens to those who invoke its name and strikes its victim in the quiet of the night. It carves up its victims, killing the lucky ones as they are free from the creature's curse. Those who survive an encounter with a kolufs krafsa must prepare for sleepless nights, tearing their hair out to the point of exhaustion as their body transforms into a new kolufs krafsa.</p>\n<h2>Two Wrongs Don't Make A Right</h2>\n<p>Some kolufs krafsas seek out werecreatures to bite them. They hope that the new curse will counteract their current one, or at the very least help them grow hair again. Sadly, they just end up doubly cursed, hairless monstrosities who roam the night without even their moral compass for consolation.</p>\n<h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2>\n<p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 30/65/125 gp</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (piercing, slashing), armor (light, medium), perception item, skill items (Athletics, Stealth)</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> constitution, energy resistant (positive), evil, strength, wild</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Strange and Unusual","authors":"Luca T. Fassari","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"creatureType":""},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.932,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":5},"dex":{"mod":3},"con":{"mod":4},"int":{"mod":2},"wis":{"mod":-2},"cha":{"mod":0}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":10,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":17,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":15,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":9,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"athletics":{"base":15},"stealth":{"base":13}},"traits":{"value":["curse","humanoid"],"rarity":"rare","size":{"value":"med"}}},"img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e/art/Portraits/kolufs-krafsa.webp","items":[{"type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","name":"Split Ends","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The kolufs krafsa is critically hit by an attack from a mammalian humanoid who possesses hair</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> Retaliating in anger for being distracted, the kolufs krafsa forces the triggering creature's hair to tear and frizz up while showing visions of its own cursed transformation into a kolufs krafsa. The triggering creature must succeed a @Check[type:will|dc:21] save or be @Compendium[pf2e.conditionitems.Frightened]{Frightened 2} and @Compendium[pf2e.conditionitems.Immobilized]{Immobilized} for 1 round.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"reaction"},"category":"defensive","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""}},"effects":[],"_id":"U05oCc0dLrNHZkOm","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"5.1.1","coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":1688836030893,"modifiedTime":1688836061142,"lastModifiedBy":"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq","compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","name":"Clinging Grab","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>The kolufs krafsa clings to its @Compendium[pf2e.conditionitems.Grabbed]{Grabbed} victim. This causes it to enter the same space as a Medium or smaller creature it has grabbed, or one square of a Large or larger creature's space. The kolufs krafsa can only have a single creature grabbed, and while the kolufs krafsa is grabbing a creature, the kolufs krafsa is @Compendium[pf2e.conditionitems.Clumsy]{Clumsy 2}.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"category":"offensive","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""}},"effects":[],"_id":"QUqefaGGiAHy6HSl","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"5.1.1","coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":1688836031565,"modifiedTime":1688836169837,"lastModifiedBy":"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq","compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","name":"Curse of the Kolufs Krafsa","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>The curse affects only mammalian humanoids.</p>\n<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> @Check[type:will|dc:21] save</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> Each night before going to sleep, the cursed creature feels their body changing, and their hair begins to feel foreign and invasive. They tear their own hair out until they fall asleep, and @Compendium[pf2e.conditionitems.Unconscious]{Unconscious}ly continue to do so as they sleep. The cursed creature takes @Damage[2d10[piercing]] damage with a @Check[type:will|dc:21|basic:true] save; this effect is nonlethal. They also awaken @Compendium[pf2e.conditionitems.Fatigued]{Fatigued}. If the curse brings the creature to 0 Hit Points, or if the creature remains cursed for a full month, the creature fully transforms into a kolufs krafsa.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["curse","occult"]},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"category":"offensive","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""}},"effects":[],"_id":"j049HQBF8vZYOBx3","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"5.3.1","coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":1688836034644,"modifiedTime":1691713280524,"lastModifiedBy":"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq","compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","name":"Tearing the Hair","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The kolufs krafsa has a mammalian humanoid who possesses hair @Compendium[pf2e.conditionitems.Grabbed]{Grabbed}</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The kolufs krafsa violently rips the hair off of the creature it has grabbed. The creature takes @Damage[2d6[piercing]] damage and [[/r 1d6[persistent,bleed]]] damage, with a @Check[type:fortitude|dc:24] save.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage and is exposed to Curse of the Kolufs Krasa.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes double damage and is exposed to Curse of the Kolufs Krasa, and the curse's initial save is @Check[type:will|dc:21|traits:curse,occult,transmutation] instead of DC 21.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigr